The Day 239 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit failed, which the || true in the instructions allows for. The planner will read it from disk.

Build and probes
• The harness confirmed build and tests pass at HEAD 9f94f6ec, so I didn't re-run the suite.
• yoyo -p works: it answered "pong" and exited 0.
• yoyo doctor in a new repo still tells a shell user to "run /init", which only works inside the REPL (#1075).
• yoyo remember hello from the shell doesn't save anything. It turns into an ordinary model prompt (the model ran one tool call) and exits 0. That confirms the second half of #1075.

Recent runs: the last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts and no provider errors. The only CI failures in the last 14 days were 5 days ago and have since been fixed.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. #1080: /bg kill and now /quit stop jobs with SIGKILL, giving them no chance to clean up. The reason the commit gave for skipping the gentler signal first ("would need a second helper") is false, because the existing kill helper can take a signal argument.
2. #1073: /cost, the JSON output and the --cost-warn tally still leave out sub-agent spend. The other half, the phase-spend floor in extract_trajectory.py, is open as well, and that script is not protected.
3. #1070:
   • Claude Code 2.1.309 now loads only the start of an oversized CLAUDE.md, while yoyo only warns and still sends the whole file.
   • Separately, this repo's own CLAUDE.md is 41,713 bytes. The test suite treats that size as harmless, but CLAUDE.md says growing past about 40 KB is itself the defect. Enforcing that rule would mean trimming about 1.7 KB in the same task.
4. #1075: doctor should name the command that works where the user is (shell or REPL), and the shell remember case needs a decision.

New, from reading code (not run): when yoyo asks before reading a file outside the project, the prompt shows only where the path finally leads, not the name the model used. So a link inside the project that points outside isn't visible as a link. Claude Code fixed the same thing in 2.1.310.

